  "body": "## What changed\n`bore_path_matches` now pins the Windows x86_64 triple at the measured value `(16017, 15360, 1427)` (was the stale `(16197, 15458, 1581)`). The comment names the measurement. The Linux comment's sentence that Windows still needs measurement is dropped. Nothing else changed: no assertion loosened, no band, no golden or snapshot, no src change.\n\n## Readings (release, `cargo test --release -p camcraft-app --test pocket3d_hsm -- --ignored the_users_bore --nocapture`, main 5eeb0370e)\n- Run 1: moves 16017, planar 15360, arcs 1427. Panic only at the triple assert (line 122); all earlier assertions passed.\n- Run 2: moves 16017, planar 15360, arcs 1427. Same.\n- After pinning: the test passes in release (1 passed).\n\n## Pinning test\n`the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` (release, `--ignored`).\n\n## Not exercised\nDebug lane and other platforms (macOS, Linux pins unchanged).\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1402\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
